IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc5-s110-4-to-117`

-- Tests for ccc5-s110-4-to-117.l4. Every expected value was decided from the text before the run; a failing assertion is a finding.

-- s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge may fix a date for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1): expected values follow the text (s 110.4(1))
#ASSERT `s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge may fix a date for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge may fix a date for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1)` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: s 110.1 an emergency prohibition order has been made
#ASSERT `s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge may fix a date for the hearing of an application under subsection 111(1)` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- s 110.1 an emergency prohibition order has been made: the other way it can fail ((JUST FALSE))

-- s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge is bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to the person: expected values follow the text (s 110.4(1))
#ASSERT `s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge is bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to the person` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge is bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to the person` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: s 110.1 an emergency prohibition order has been made
#ASSERT `s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge is bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to the person` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the judge has fixed a date for the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1)
#ASSERT `s 110.4(1) the provincial court judge is bound to direct that notice of the hearing be given to the person` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- s 110.1 an emergency prohibition order has been made: the other way it can fail ((JUST FALSE))

-- s 110.4(2)(a) the application for the order under subsection 110.1(3) is deemed an application made under subsection 111(1): expected values follow the text (s 110.4(2)(a))
#ASSERT `s 110.4(2)(a) the application for the order under subsection 110.1(3) is deemed an application made under subsection 111(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 110.4(2)(a) the application for the order under subsection 110.1(3) is deemed an application made under subsection 111(1)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the application is the application for the order referred to in subsection 110.1(3)
#ASSERT `s 110.4(2)(a) the application for the order under subsection 110.1(3) is deemed an application made under subsection 111(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: the purpose is the purpose of subsection 111(2)


-- s 110.4(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant
#ASSERT `s 110.4(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant` TRUE Ontario EQUALS JUST `the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province`
#ASSERT `s 110.4(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant` TRUE `British Columbia` EQUALS JUST `the Attorney General or Solicitor General of the province`
#ASSERT `s 110.4(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant` TRUE Yukon EQUALS JUST `the Attorney General of Canada`   -- "if the application was made in a territory, the Attorney General of Canada"
#ASSERT `s 110.4(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant` TRUE `Northwest Territories` EQUALS JUST `the Attorney General of Canada`
#ASSERT `s 110.4(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant` TRUE Nunavut EQUALS JUST `the Attorney General of Canada`
#ASSERT `s 110.4(2)(b) the Attorney General who becomes the applicant` FALSE Ontario EQUALS NOTHING   -- a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer applied: the paragraph does not change the applicant


-- s 110.4(3) the date fixed for the hearing is before the end of the period of the order: "before the end of the period": read as strictly before the day the period ends (fork register)
#ASSERT `s 110.4(3) the date fixed for the hearing is before the end of the period of the order` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 110.4(3) the date fixed for the hearing is before the end of the period of the order` (Date 9 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day before the period ends
#ASSERT `s 110.4(3) the date fixed for the hearing is before the end of the period of the order` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- on the day the period ends is not "before" it
#ASSERT `s 110.4(3) the date fixed for the hearing is before the end of the period of the order` (Date 11 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 110.4(3) the provincial court judge may adjourn the hearing: expected values follow the text (s 110.4(3))
#ASSERT `s 110.4(3) the provincial court judge may adjourn the hearing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 110.4(3) the provincial court judge may adjourn the hearing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 110.4(3) the provincial court judge may adjourn the hearing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is of the where, when or upon kind, so the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (test 3(i)) lists the function and leaves the answer as the guide's ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 gives it: JUST FALSE, not NOTHING (element missing: the application to adjourn is made by the applicant or by the person against whom an order under subsection 111(5) is sought)
#ASSERT `s 110.4(3) the provincial court judge may adjourn the hearing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 110.4(3) the provincial court judge may adjourn the hearing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is of the where, when or upon kind, so the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (test 3(i)) lists the function and leaves the answer as the guide's ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 gives it: JUST FALSE, not NOTHING (element missing: the application is made before or at any time during the hearing)

-- s 110.4(4) the provincial court judge is bound to cause notice to be served on the Attorney General: expected values follow the text (s 110.4(4))
#ASSERT `s 110.4(4) the provincial court judge is bound to cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 110.4(4) the provincial court judge is bound to cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the Attorney General becomes, under paragraph (2)(b), the applicant in an application made under subsection 111(1)


-- s 110.4(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed
#ASSERT `s 110.4(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- exactly 15 days before: "not later than 15 days before"
#ASSERT `s 110.4(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` (Date 20 2 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- earlier than 15 days before
#ASSERT `s 110.4(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` (Date 2 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- 14 days before is too late
#ASSERT `s 110.4(4) the notice was served not later than 15 days before the date fixed` (Date 16 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- on the day itself
-- the regulative rule, run (a trace prints its outcome; it cannot be asserted on the stable binary). Hearing fixed 30 days ahead: notice due by day 15.
#TRACE `s 110.4(4) the judge must cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a provincial court judge` DOES `s 110.4(4) cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` AT 15
#TRACE `s 110.4(4) the judge must cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a provincial court judge` DOES `s 110.4(4) cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` AT 16
#TRACE `s 110.4(4) the judge must cause notice to be served on the Attorney General` 30 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 16

-- s 110.4(5) the provincial court judge is bound to cancel the hearing: expected values follow the text (s 110.4(5))
#ASSERT `s 110.4(5) the provincial court judge is bound to cancel the hearing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 110.4(5) the provincial court judge is bound to cancel the hearing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the judge revokes an order made under subsection 110.1(3) against the person
#ASSERT `s 110.4(5) the provincial court judge is bound to cancel the hearing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the application for an order sought under subsection 111(5) against the person has not yet been heard

-- s 111(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing weapons: expected values follow the text (s 111(1))
#ASSERT `s 111(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing weapons` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 111(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing weapons` NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: s 2 peace officer: the applicant is one / the applicant is a firearms officer / the applicant is a chief firearms officer
#ASSERT `s 111(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing weapons` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: s 2 peace officer: the applicant is one
#ASSERT `s 111(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing weapons` NOTHING TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the applicant is a firearms officer
#ASSERT `s 111(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing weapons` NOTHING FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the applicant is a chief firearms officer
#ASSERT `s 111(1) a peace officer, firearms officer or chief firearms officer may apply to a provincial court judge for an order prohibiting a person from possessing weapons` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the applicant believes on reasonable grounds that it is not desirable in the interests of the safety of the person against whom the order is sought or of any other person that the person against whom the order is sought should possess any such thing

-- s 111(2) the provincial court judge is bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice be given to the person: expected values follow the text (s 111(2))
#ASSERT `s 111(2) the provincial court judge is bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice be given to the person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 111(2) the provincial court judge is bound to fix a date for the hearing and direct that notice be given to the person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: an application has been made under subsection 111(1)

-- s 111(3) the provincial court judge is bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person: expected values follow the text (s 111(3))
#ASSERT `s 111(3) the provincial court judge is bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 111(3) the provincial court judge is bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the hearing of an application made under subsection 111(1) is held
#ASSERT `s 111(3) the provincial court judge is bound to hear all relevant evidence presented by or on behalf of the applicant and the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the judge proceeds ex parte under subsection (4)

-- s 111(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application: expected values follow the text (s 111(4))
#ASSERT `s 111(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 111(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the application is made under subsection 111(1)
#ASSERT `s 111(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the person against whom the order is sought is absent
#ASSERT `s 111(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: Part XXVII the circumstances are those in which a summary conviction court may proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant
#ASSERT `s 111(4) the provincial court judge may proceed ex parte to hear and determine the application` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING   -- Part XXVII the circumstances are those in which a summary conviction court may proceed with a trial in the absence of the defendant: the other way it can fail ((JUST FALSE))

-- s 111(5) the provincial court judge is bound to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing the things: expected values follow the text (s 111(5))
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the provincial court judge is bound to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing the things` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the provincial court judge is bound to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing the things` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the hearing of an application made under subsection (1) has concluded
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the provincial court judge is bound to make an order prohibiting the person from possessing the things` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the judge is satisfied that the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist


-- s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years: a period is compared in calendar months first; days count only when the months already equal sixty (NOTES.md, fork register)
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF 3, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF 4, 11, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- one month short of five years
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- exactly five years: "not exceeding"
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 0, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- five years less a day
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF 0, 18, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- eighteen months
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF 5, 0, 1, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- five years and a day exceeds five years
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF 5, 1, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the period of the order is not more than five years` (`Length of time` OF 6, 0, 0, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the order begins on the day on which it is made` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 111(5) the order begins on the day on which it is made` (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a period that begins another day is not what the text says

-- s 111(6) the provincial court judge is bound to include a statement of reasons in the record: expected values follow the text (s 111(6))
#ASSERT `s 111(6) the provincial court judge is bound to include a statement of reasons in the record` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 111(6) the provincial court judge is bound to include a statement of reasons in the record` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the judge does not make an order under subsection (1) / the judge makes an order but does not prohibit the possession of everything referred to in subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 111(6) the provincial court judge is bound to include a statement of reasons in the record` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the judge does not make an order under subsection (1)
#ASSERT `s 111(6) the provincial court judge is bound to include a statement of reasons in the record` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the judge makes an order but does not prohibit the possession of everything referred to in subsection (1)


-- s 111(7) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number: R1 of PLAN.md, a range of section numbers tested against the core record
#ASSERT `s 111(7) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 113, "(1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 111(7) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 115, "(1.1)") EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 111(7) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 117, "") EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last section named
#ASSERT `s 111(7) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 112, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- before the range
#ASSERT `s 111(7) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` TRUE (`Provision of the Code` OF 117.01, "(1)") EQUALS NOTHING   -- after the range
#ASSERT `s 111(7) sections 113 to 117 apply to the order, tested by section number` FALSE (`Provision of the Code` OF 114, "") EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an order under subsection (5)

-- s 111(8) the person to whom the order relates, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the superior court against the order: expected values follow the text (s 111(8))
#ASSERT `s 111(8) the person to whom the order relates, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the superior court against the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 111(8) the person to whom the order relates, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the superior court against the order` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the appellant is the person to whom the order relates / the appellant is the Attorney General
#ASSERT `s 111(8) the person to whom the order relates, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the superior court against the order` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the appellant is the person to whom the order relates
#ASSERT `s 111(8) the person to whom the order relates, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the superior court against the order` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the appellant is the Attorney General
#ASSERT `s 111(8) the person to whom the order relates, or the Attorney General, may appeal to the superior court against the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: the provincial court judge makes an order under subsection (5)

-- s 111(9) the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the decision not to make an order: expected values follow the text (s 111(9))
#ASSERT `s 111(9) the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the decision not to make an order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 111(9) the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the decision not to make an order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the appellant is the Attorney General
#ASSERT `s 111(9) the Attorney General may appeal to the superior court against the decision not to make an order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: the provincial court judge does not make an order under subsection (5)


-- s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal: sections 785-812, 816-819 and 829-838 are excepted; every other provision of Part XXVII applies "with such modifications as the circumstances require"
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 813 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- 813 is not in an excepted range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 815 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last section before the 816-819 range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 820 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the first section after the 816-819 range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 828 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last section before the 829-838 range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 839 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the first section after the 829-838 range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 785 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- first section of the first excepted range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 812 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- last section of the first excepted range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 816 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- first section of the second excepted range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 819 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- last section of the second excepted range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 829 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- first section of the third excepted range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 838 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- last section of the third excepted range
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 813 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a provision of Part XXVII
#ASSERT `s 111(10) the provision of Part XXVII applies to the appeal` 813 TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an appeal under the subsections named

-- s 112 a provincial court judge may revoke the order: expected values follow the text (s 112)
#ASSERT `s 112 a provincial court judge may revoke the order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 112 a provincial court judge may revoke the order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the judge is satisfied that the circumstances for which the order was made have ceased to exist
#ASSERT `s 112 a provincial court judge may revoke the order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 112 a provincial court judge may revoke the order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is of the where, when or upon kind, so the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (test 3(i)) lists the function and leaves the answer as the guide's ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 gives it: JUST FALSE, not NOTHING (exception: the application is made by the person against whom an order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or 111(5))

-- s 113(1) the competent authority may make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for sustenance or employment: expected values follow the text (s 113(1))
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the competent authority may make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for sustenance or employment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the competent authority may make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for sustenance or employment` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the person is or will be a person against whom a prohibition order is made
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the competent authority may make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for sustenance or employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the person establishes to the satisfaction of the competent authority that the person needs a firearm or restricted weapon to hunt or trap in order to sustain the person or the person's family / the person establishes to the satisfaction of the competent authority that a prohibition order against the person would constitute a virtual prohibition against employment in the only vocation open to the person
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the competent authority may make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for sustenance or employment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the person establishes to the satisfaction of the competent authority that the person needs a firearm or restricted weapon to hunt or trap in order to sustain the person or the person's family
#ASSERT `s 113(1) the competent authority may make an order authorizing a licence, authorization or registration certificate for sustenance or employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the person establishes to the satisfaction of the competent authority that a prohibition order against the person would constitute a virtual prohibition against employment in the only vocation open to the person

-- s 113(2) the competent authority may make an order under subsection (1) only after taking the factors into account: expected values follow the text (s 113(2))
#ASSERT `s 113(2) the competent authority may make an order under subsection (1) only after taking the factors into account` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 113(2) the competent authority may make an order under subsection (1) only after taking the factors into account` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the competent authority has taken into account the criminal record, if any, of the person
#ASSERT `s 113(2) the competent authority may make an order under subsection (1) only after taking the factors into account` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the competent authority has taken into account the nature and circumstances of the offence, if any, in respect of which the prohibition order was or will be made
#ASSERT `s 113(2) the competent authority may make an order under subsection (1) only after taking the factors into account` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the competent authority has taken into account the safety of the person and of other persons

-- s 113(3)(a) an authorization, licence or registration certificate is barred from being denied solely on the basis of the prohibition order or the offence: expected values follow the text (s 113(3)(a))
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(a) an authorization, licence or registration certificate is barred from being denied solely on the basis of the prohibition order or the offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(a) an authorization, licence or registration certificate is barred from being denied solely on the basis of the prohibition order or the offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the denial is solely on the basis of a prohibition order against the person or the commission of an offence in respect of which a prohibition order was made against the person
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(a) an authorization, licence or registration certificate is barred from being denied solely on the basis of the prohibition order or the offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: an order is made under subsection (1)

-- s 113(3)(b) the authorization or licence may be issued to the person for the duration of the order: expected values follow the text (s 113(3)(b))
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(b) the authorization or licence may be issued to the person for the duration of the order` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(b) the authorization or licence may be issued to the person for the duration of the order` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 113(3)(b) the authorization or licence may be issued to the person for the duration of the order` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING; the gate is of the where, when or upon kind, so the name-test sweep of 2026-11-12 (test 3(i)) lists the function and leaves the answer as the guide's ruling (b) of 2026-11-05 gives it: JUST FALSE, not NOTHING (element missing: an order is made under subsection (1))
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(b) the authorization or licence may be issued to the person for the duration of the order` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: the authorization or licence is issued for sustenance or employment purposes
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(b) the authorization or licence may be issued to the person for the duration of the order` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: the order sets out terms and conditions and the issue is not in accordance with them

-- s 113(3)(b) the chief firearms officer may attach further terms and conditions to the authorization or licence: expected values follow the text (s 113(3)(b))
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(b) the chief firearms officer may attach further terms and conditions to the authorization or licence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(b) the chief firearms officer may attach further terms and conditions to the authorization or licence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the further terms and conditions are not inconsistent with the purpose for which the authorization or licence is issued
#ASSERT `s 113(3)(b) the chief firearms officer may attach further terms and conditions to the authorization or licence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the further terms and conditions are not inconsistent with any terms and conditions set out in the order

-- s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings: expected values follow the text (s 113(4))
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the proceedings are for an order under subsection 109(1) / the proceedings are for an order under subsection 110(1) / the proceedings are for an order under subsection 110.1(3) / the proceedings are for an order under subsection 111(5) / the proceedings are for an order under subsection 117.05(4) / the proceedings are for an order under subsection 515(2) / the proceedings are for an order under paragraph 732.1(3)(d) / the proceedings are for an order under section 810 / the proceedings are for an order under section 810.03
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the proceedings are for an order under subsection 109(1)
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the proceedings are for an order under subsection 110(1)
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the proceedings are for an order under subsection 110.1(3)
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the proceedings are for an order under subsection 111(5)
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the proceedings are for an order under subsection 117.05(4)
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the proceedings are for an order under subsection 515(2)
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the proceedings are for an order under paragraph 732.1(3)(d)
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the proceedings are for an order under section 810
#ASSERT `s 113(4) an order under subsection (1) may be made during the proceedings` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the proceedings are for an order under section 810.03

-- s 113(5) competent authority: expected values follow the text (s 113(5))
#ASSERT `s 113(5) competent authority` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 113(5) competent authority` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the authority made the prohibition order or has jurisdiction to make it

-- s 114 the competent authority may require the person to surrender the things and documents: expected values follow the text (s 114)
#ASSERT `s 114 the competent authority may require the person to surrender the things and documents` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 114 the competent authority may require the person to surrender the things and documents` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the authority makes a prohibition order against the person
#ASSERT `s 114 the competent authority may require the person to surrender the things and documents` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the thing is in the person's possession on the commencement of the order and its possession is prohibited by the order / the authorization, licence or registration certificate relates to a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order and is held by the person on the commencement of the order
#ASSERT `s 114 the competent authority may require the person to surrender the things and documents` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the thing is in the person's possession on the commencement of the order and its possession is prohibited by the order
#ASSERT `s 114 the competent authority may require the person to surrender the things and documents` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the authorization, licence or registration certificate relates to a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the order and is held by the person on the commencement of the order

-- s 114 the authority is bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering: expected values follow the text (s 114)
#ASSERT `s 114 the authority is bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 114 the authority is bound to specify in the order a reasonable period for surrendering` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the authority requires the person in the order to surrender things or documents

-- s 114 section 117.01 does not apply to the person during the specified period: expected values follow the text (s 114)
#ASSERT `s 114 section 117.01 does not apply to the person during the specified period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 114 section 117.01 does not apply to the person during the specified period` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the order requires the person to surrender things or documents and specifies a reasonable period for it
#ASSERT `s 114 section 117.01 does not apply to the person during the specified period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the day is within the period specified in the order

-- s 115(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the order: expected values follow the text (s 115(1.1))
#ASSERT `s 115(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 115(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the order` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the order is made under subsection 110.1(3) / the order is made under section 515
#ASSERT `s 115(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the order is made under subsection 110.1(3)
#ASSERT `s 115(1.1) subsection (1) does not apply to the order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the order is made under section 515

-- s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty: expected values follow the text (s 115(1))
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the thing is one the possession of which is prohibited by the prohibition order
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: on the commencement of the order the thing is in the person's possession / on the commencement of the order the thing has been seized and detained by, or surrendered to, a peace officer
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: on the commencement of the order the thing is in the person's possession
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: on the commencement of the order the thing has been seized and detained by, or surrendered to, a peace officer
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: the prohibition order specifies otherwise
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exception: the answer of s 115(1.1)

-- s 115(2) the thing forfeited is to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs: expected values follow the text (s 115(2))
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the thing forfeited is to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the thing forfeited is to be disposed of or otherwise dealt with as the Attorney General directs` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection (1)

-- s 116(1) the authorization, licence or registration certificate is revoked or amended on the commencement of the prohibition order: expected values follow the text (s 116(1))
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the authorization, licence or registration certificate is revoked or amended on the commencement of the prohibition order` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the authorization, licence or registration certificate is revoked or amended on the commencement of the prohibition order` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: the authorization, licence or registration certificate relates to a thing the possession of which is prohibited by the prohibition order
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the authorization, licence or registration certificate is revoked or amended on the commencement of the prohibition order` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- element missing: it was issued to the person against whom the prohibition order is made

-- s 116(2) the authorization, licence or registration certificate remains revoked or amended: expected values follow the text (s 116(2))
#ASSERT `s 116(2) the authorization, licence or registration certificate remains revoked or amended` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 116(2) the authorization, licence or registration certificate remains revoked or amended` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the order is made under subsection 110.1(3) or section 515
#ASSERT `s 116(2) the authorization, licence or registration certificate remains revoked or amended` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the day is within the period during which the order is in force

-- s 117 the competent authority is bound to order the thing returned to the owner, or its proceeds or value paid: expected values follow the text (s 117)
#ASSERT `s 117 the competent authority is bound to order the thing returned to the owner, or its proceeds or value paid` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every element of the provision present
#ASSERT `s 117 the competent authority is bound to order the thing returned to the owner, or its proceeds or value paid` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the authority is satisfied, on application for an order under this section, that a person other than the person against whom a prohibition order was or will be made applies
#ASSERT `s 117 the competent authority is bound to order the thing returned to the owner, or its proceeds or value paid` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the person is the owner of a thing that is or may be forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection 115(1) and is lawfully entitled to possess it
#ASSERT `s 117 the competent authority is bound to order the thing returned to the owner, or its proceeds or value paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- element missing: the prohibition order is an order under subsection 109(1) or 110(1) / the person had no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of the offence in respect of which the prohibition order was made
#ASSERT `s 117 the competent authority is bound to order the thing returned to the owner, or its proceeds or value paid` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the prohibition order is an order under subsection 109(1) or 110(1)
#ASSERT `s 117 the competent authority is bound to order the thing returned to the owner, or its proceeds or value paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- alternative present: the person had no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of the offence in respect of which the prohibition order was made


-- s 117 what the order for the owner is
#ASSERT `s 117 what the order for the owner is` `s 117 the thing still exists` EQUALS `s 117 the thing is returned to the owner`
#ASSERT `s 117 what the order for the owner is` `s 117 the thing was sold` EQUALS `s 117 the proceeds of the sale are paid to the owner`
#ASSERT `s 117 what the order for the owner is` `s 117 the thing was destroyed` EQUALS `s 117 an amount equal to the value of the thing is paid to the owner`
